# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where this deployment thinks it lives
#
# Canonicals, Open Graph URLs and the sitemap are built from this. Leave it
# unset on the real domain. On ANY other host (a Vercel preview, staging) set
# it to that host — robots.ts then disallows crawlers outright, so the copy
# cannot be indexed or compete with tfsuncons.com.qa.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://tfs-suncons.vercel.app"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trade enquiry form delivery
#
# The form at /contact#enquiry posts to /api/enquiry. That route validates the
# submission server-side and then delivers it by ONE of the routes below.
#
# If neither is configured the API returns 503 and the form shows a real error
# with the phone number and email as a fallback. It never fakes a success.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Option 1 — post the enquiry straight into a lead pipeline.
# This can point at the VBP lead-management backend so website enquiries land
# on the same dashboard as the WhatsApp leads.
# ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL="https://your-backend.example.com/api/leads/website"
# ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_TOKEN="a-shared-secret"

# Option 2 — email the enquiry (https://resend.com).
# RESEND_API_KEY="re_xxxxxxxxxxxx"
# ENQUIRY_TO_EMAIL="info@tfsuncons.com.qa"
# ENQUIRY_FROM_EMAIL="website@tfsuncons.com.qa"
